<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia cabinet to discuss jobs, no action now.</title>
<headline>Australia cabinet to discuss jobs, no action now.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian government's cabinet has started a day-long meeting in Sydney on Tuesday to discuss ways to tackle high unemployment, but cannot take any immediate action because Prime Minister John Howard was still at home sick, a cabinet minister said.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be no immediate decisions, but of course the government is working on this issue in a concerted way on a number of fronts endlessly,&quot; Science and Technology Minister Peter McGuaran told reporters as he entered the meeting.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
